  "prompt": "=== Chain-of-thought analysis prompt ===\nYou are a software requirements analyst preparing a UML state machine model.\n\nAnalyze the requirement and extract only the modeling facts needed for a state transition diagram. Keep the analysis concise and evidence-based.\n\nReturn the analysis using exactly these headings:\nStates:\nInitial state:\nFinal states:\nEvents or conditions:\nTransitions:\nMissing or ambiguous details:\n\nDo not write PlantUML in this step.\n\nRequirement:\nOnline Quiz System — Polished Requirement Specification\n\nFunctional Requirements\n1. The system shall allow users to register or log in with their details.\n2. The system shall allow users to continue as a teacher or a student after logging in.\n3. The system shall allow teachers to create a new quiz.\n4. The system shall allow teachers to edit an existing quiz.\n5. The system shall allow teachers to save a quiz as a draft or post it for students after working on it.\n6. The system shall allow teachers to view quiz results once the quiz is over.\n7. The system shall allow students to select a quiz after getting notified if they continue as a student.\n8. The system shall allow students to answer the selected quiz.\n9. The system shall allow students to submit their quiz after answering.\n10. The system shall allow students to view the result after submitting the quiz.\n\n=== Chain-of-thought analysis response ===\nStates:\nLogged Out, Logged In (Teacher), Logged In (Student), Quiz Creation, Quiz Editing, Quiz Draft, Quiz Posted, Quiz Taking, Quiz Result Viewing\n\nInitial state:\nLogged Out\n\nFinal states:\nQuiz Result Viewing (for Student), Logged Out (after logout)\n\nEvents or conditions:\nRegistration, Login, Select Role (Teacher/Student), Create Quiz, Edit Quiz, Save Draft, Post Quiz, Quiz Started, Answer Question, Submit Quiz, Quiz Over, View Results, Logout\n\nTransitions:\nLogged Out -> Logged In (Teacher) [Login, Select Role (Teacher)]\nLogged Out -> Logged In (Student) [Login, Select Role (Student)]\nLogged In (Teacher) -> Quiz Creation [Create Quiz]\nQuiz Creation -> Quiz Editing [Edit Quiz]\nQuiz Editing -> Quiz Draft [Save Draft]\nQuiz Draft -> Quiz Posted [Post Quiz]\nLogged In (Student) -> Quiz Taking [Select Quiz, Quiz Started]\nQuiz Taking -> Submit Quiz [Answer Question, Submit Quiz]\nSubmit Quiz -> Quiz Result Viewing [Quiz Over]\nQuiz Result Viewing -> Logged Out [Logout]\nQuiz Result Viewing -> Logged In (Student) [Select Quiz, Quiz Started]\n\nMissing or ambiguous details:\n* Specific actions required for registration.\n* Details of quiz notification to students.\n* How quiz selection is presented to students.\n* The process of answering questions (e.g., time limits, question types).\n* The format and content of quiz results.\n* Error handling and invalid state transitions (e.g., what happens if a teacher tries to take a quiz).\n* Security considerations around quiz access and data.\n\n=== PlantUML generation prompt ===\nYou are a UML modeling expert.\n\nConvert the requirement and the structured analysis into one UML state transition diagram in PlantUML format.\n\nOutput Rules:\n- Generate ONLY valid PlantUML code.\n- Start with @startuml and end with @enduml.\n- Use [*] for exactly one initial transition.\n- Include at least one final transition to [*].\n- Use clear transition labels when requirement evidence exists.\n- Do not include explanations, analysis, or markdown fences.\n\nRequirement:\nOnline Quiz System — Polished Requirement Specification\n\nFunctional Requirements\n1. The system shall allow users to register or log in with their details.\n2. The system shall allow users to continue as a teacher or a student after logging in.\n3. The system shall allow teachers to create a new quiz.\n4. The system shall allow teachers to edit an existing quiz.\n5. The system shall allow teachers to save a quiz as a draft or post it for students after working on it.\n6. The system shall allow teachers to view quiz results once the quiz is over.\n7. The system shall allow students to select a quiz after getting notified if they continue as a student.\n8. The system shall allow students to answer the selected quiz.\n9. The system shall allow students to submit their quiz after answering.\n10. The system shall allow students to view the result after submitting the quiz.\n\nStructured analysis from step 1:\nStates:\nLogged Out, Logged In (Teacher), Logged In (Student), Quiz Creation, Quiz Editing, Quiz Draft, Quiz Posted, Quiz Taking, Quiz Result Viewing\n\nInitial state:\nLogged Out\n\nFinal states:\nQuiz Result Viewing (for Student), Logged Out (after logout)\n\nEvents or conditions:\nRegistration, Login, Select Role (Teacher/Student), Create Quiz, Edit Quiz, Save Draft, Post Quiz, Quiz Started, Answer Question, Submit Quiz, Quiz Over, View Results, Logout\n\nTransitions:\nLogged Out -> Logged In (Teacher) [Login, Select Role (Teacher)]\nLogged Out -> Logged In (Student) [Login, Select Role (Student)]\nLogged In (Teacher) -> Quiz Creation [Create Quiz]\nQuiz Creation -> Quiz Editing [Edit Quiz]\nQuiz Editing -> Quiz Draft [Save Draft]\nQuiz Draft -> Quiz Posted [Post Quiz]\nLogged In (Student) -> Quiz Taking [Select Quiz, Quiz Started]\nQuiz Taking -> Submit Quiz [Answer Question, Submit Quiz]\nSubmit Quiz -> Quiz Result Viewing [Quiz Over]\nQuiz Result Viewing -> Logged Out [Logout]\nQuiz Result Viewing -> Logged In (Student) [Select Quiz, Quiz Started]\n\nMissing or ambiguous details:\n* Specific actions required for registration.\n* Details of quiz notification to students.\n* How quiz selection is presented to students.\n* The process of answering questions (e.g., time limits, question types).\n* The format and content of quiz results.\n* Error handling and invalid state transitions (e.g., what happens if a teacher tries to take a quiz).\n* Security considerations around quiz access and data.\n\nNow return only the final PlantUML.\n",
